# 18. HEADLESS AGENT FLOW

MonoES also supports a headless-agent authentication flow.

Do NOT use this for normal user browser login.

Reserve it for future server/agent use cases.

Documented workflow:

```text
POST /api/auth/agent/claim

POST /api/auth/agent/claim/verify
```

The first request accepts:

```json
{
  "email": "...",
  "client_id": "...",
  "scope": "..."
}
```

The user receives a six-digit code by email.

Verification accepts:

```json
{
  "email": "...",
  "code": "...",
  "client_id": "..."
}
```

Successful verification returns an access token.

Do not implement this in the initial MVP unless there is a concrete agent use case requiring browserless authentication.

---

# 19. HEADLESS SECURITY CHARACTERISTICS

If implemented later, account for documented MonoES behavior:

- codes expire after 10 minutes;
- codes permit at most 5 attempts;
- claim requests are limited to 3 outstanding requests per email per hour;
- account lookup does not disclose whether an email exists;
- resulting token behaves like a normal OAuth-issued bearer token.

Do not weaken these protections in our UI.

