# 22. FIRST AUTHENTICATION ACCEPTANCE CRITERION

Authentication phase is DONE when:

1. `pnpm monoes:register` can register a development OAuth client.
2. `MONOES_CLIENT_ID` can be configured.
3. User visits `/login`.
4. User clicks "Continue with MonoES".
5. Browser redirects to MonoES.
6. User authenticates/approves access.
7. MonoES redirects to our callback.
8. PKCE authorization code exchange succeeds.
9. Platform resolves the user's MonoES identity.
10. Local user/account is created.
11. Local organization is created on first login.
12. Local HttpOnly session is established.
13. User lands on `/dashboard`.
14. Protected routes reject unauthenticated sessions.
15. Logout removes the local session.
16. No password is ever handled by our avatar platform.

Do not mark Phase 1 complete until this has been tested against the real MonoES authorization server at least once outside CI.